{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794169487,"nonce":"gnKs2jUTrKjnsSNe/ToVgmgSgXg=","title":"The iOS simulator loads no system fonts: SF, its weights and the generic families are missing","message":"On the iOS simulator (iPhone 15 Pro Max, iOS 17.5 runtime) mobile/example draws only part of its text: the subtitle, section headings, button labels and the input's text are missing, and bold text draws in the regular face. The log shows why: the iOS runner looks for fonts at /System/Library/Fonts/Core/... and /System/Library/Fonts/CoreUI/..., which do not exist inside the simulator runtime, and the registry then fails to preload System, SansSerif, Serif and Monospace.\n\nThis makes the simulator useless for checking text rendering, which is where it would help most (it can be screenshotted, a phone cannot).\n\nLikely fix: resolve system faces through CoreText (CTFontCreateWithName and kCTFontURLAttribute, or loading the font data from a CTFont) rather than hard-coded paths, which would also cover 1cda357. The device keeps working because its paths exist.\n\nBuilding for the simulator also needs LIBRARY_SEARCH_PATHS='$(PROJECT_DIR)/libs/simulator' on the Release configuration, which otherwise links the device library.","files":null}]}